WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:04.290
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:10.480
In this series, we have studied fluid simulations
extensively. But we haven't talked about one

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:17.270
important quantity that describes a fluid,
and this quantity is none other than viscosity.

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:20.720
Viscosity means the resistance of a fluid
against deformation.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:26.800
The large viscosity of honey makes it highly
resistant to deformation, and this is responsible

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:30.050
for its famous and beautiful coiling effect.

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:36.270
Water, however, does not have a lot of objections
against deformations, making it so easy to

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:38.470
pour it into a glass.

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:43.240
With this piece of work, it is possible to
efficiently simulate the motion of fluids,

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:52.230
and it supports the simulation of a large
range of viscosities.

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:57.390
Viscosities can also change in time. For instance,
physicists know that raising the temperature

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:02.680
will make the viscosity of fluids decrease,
which leads to melting, therefore decreasing

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:10.050
the viscosity in time will lead to a simulation
result that looks exactly like melting.

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:15.140
The technique also supports two-way coupling
where the objects have effects on the fluid

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:18.610
and vice versa.

00:01:18.610 --> 00:01:23.620
One can also put multiple fluids with different
densities and viscosities into the same domain

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:29.140
and see how they duke it out.
This is exactly what people need in the industry:

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:34.659
robust techniques that work for small and
large scale simulations with multiple objects,

00:01:34.659 --> 00:01:41.210
and material settings that can possibly change
in time.

00:01:41.210 --> 00:01:44.990
Thanks for watching and for your generous
support, and I'll see you next time!

